#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""omp-manager / ompagy - Antigravity quota dashboard for omp.

Reads `omp usage --json`, merges duplicated shared meters, scores every
account, and prints a ranked table:

    columns: Gemini 5h | Gemini 1w | Claude&GPT 5h | Claude&GPT 1w
    cells:   remaining bar + % left + time until reset
    rows:    every authenticated account, best -> worst

Data-driven: accounts and meters are discovered from the report, so adding
an account (or a new meter) later needs no code change.

The script answers to two names: `omp-manager` and `ompagy`. It detects
which one was invoked (argv[0], or the OMP_DEFAULT_PROG override) and
adapts its program name, environment variable prefix and cache directory
accordingly. Both names expose the exact same feature set.
"""

